   "output": {
    "title": "关于新台式机组装的建议，充分利用我现有的两块R9700卡",
    "summary": "作者已购两张R9700 AI PRO（每张32GB VRAM），当前主板PCIe通道拆分不足、RAM仅32GB限制性能。计划升级到X870E主板+64~128GB DDR5，考虑是否值得投入。痛点在于Vulkan/tensor splitting拖慢预填充与生成速度，P2P并行效果不稳定。",
    "reason": "社区技术帖，双R9700 AI PRO组网升级思路清晰，对相似硬件困境读者有参考价值，但非深度分析文章。"
   },
   "reference": "<!-- SC_OFF --><div class=\"md\"><p>I started out my LLM / AI journey before I really knew what I was getting into. When I fell in love with the tech, I grabbed an R9700 AI PRO card (32gb vram) and then found one a month later as an open box special, which I grabbed. This was several months ago now.</p> <p><strong>The issue:</strong> I&#39;m currently using these two cards in a board that doesn&#39;t have proper PCI-E lane splitting. I also don&#39;t have enough RAM (32gb DDR5). CPU is a Ryzen 5 7600, so not great but paired with the proper chipset and mobo, it should be able to handle PCIE-8x / 8x. However, if upgrading the CPU would help with some layers offloaded to CPU-RAM MoE model performance, I&#39;d consider it.</p> <p>I&#39;m not willing to go threadripper; it&#39;s just too damn expensive. But I might have an opportunity to switch out my motherboard and case, upgrade RAM and keep everything else. I know RAM is crazy expensive right now, but I don&#39;t see any price drops in the near future; just increases.</p> <p><strong>My thought:</strong> Upgrade motherboard to ASUS ProArt X870E-CREATOR WiFi AMD AM5 X870E or something equivalent by Asrock, etc. Upgrade RAM to 128gb DDR5 (the biggest cost increase, might not be worth it; may just go with 64gb RAM in a two-dimm config).</p> <p>My worry is that this won&#39;t be a huge step up from my current setup. Right now, I&#39;m left struggling with vulkan and tensor splitting which slows down my pre-fill and generation speeds. P2P / tensor parallelism is possible with a custom fork of llama-cpp but I have mixed results and many issues with it and it&#39;s not true PCI-E lane 8x lane splitting.</p> <p>Advice would be most welcomed.</p> </div><!-- SC_ON --> &#32; submitted by &#32; <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/user/Jorlen\"> /u/Jorlen </a> &#32; to &#32; <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/LocalLLaMA/\"> r/LocalLLaMA </a> <br/> <span><a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/LocalLLaMA/comments/1wju218/advice_on_a_new_desktop_build_to_take_advantage/\">[link]</a></span> &#32; <span><a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/LocalLLaMA/comments/1wju218/advice_on_a_new_desktop_build_to_take_advantage/\">[comments]</a></span>",
   "ref_field": "content_html",
